# ==============================================================================
# Here we are looking for obfuscation patterns
#
# Detects text obfuscated with zero-width Unicode characters
# Common in phishing emails to bypass spam filters
#
# Zero-width characters used by spammers:
# U+200B (Zero Width Space)
# U+200C (Zero Width Non-Joiner)
# U+200D (Zero Width Joiner)
# U+FEFF (Zero Width No-Break Space / BOM)
# 
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Language: any
# Weight:   12.0
# ==============================================================================

# Topics
# ==============================================================================

# Generic pattern: detects 3+ letters with zero-width chars between them
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Matches obfuscated words regardless of content
# Using actual UTF-8 characters for Hyperscan compatibility

/[a-z][​‌‍﻿][a-z][​‌‍﻿][a-z]/i 0.1

# Soft Hyphen obfuscation (HTML &shy; = U+00AD)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spammers insert soft hyphens to break up words: me&shy;ssage&shy;s
/[a-z][­][a-z][­][a-z]/i

# 
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Sample: HOf‏fene B‏estätig‏ung zu Ihr‏em K‏onto
/‏[a-z\s]{4,15}‏[a-z\s]{4,15}‏/i

# Narrow, targeted masking patterns for Japanese phrases.
# These are intentionally constrained to known word fragments to avoid broad
# false positives from arbitrary Unicode separator insertion.
/ご(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})注(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})文(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})内(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})容/i
/ご(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})注(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})文(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})商(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})品/i
/配(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})送(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})担(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})当(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})業(?:[﻿‍⁠]{0,3})者/i

